{
 "summary": "Checkout is failing because inventory POST /reserve is slow (p95 ~4.76s, ~2.5s of trace self time), so orders times out reserving inventory and returns 504, and the gateway then returns 502. The gateway deploy (1.4.2 -> 1.5.4 at 00:45:44Z) happened after the errors had already started at window start, and the gateway logged the same error under both releases. That makes the deploy an unlikely cause.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory POST /reserve (release 3.1.5) is slow and accounts for the dominant self time in failing traces. Orders times out waiting on it ('timed out reserving inventory') and returns 504, which the gateway surfaces as 502. Inventory itself reports no 5xx, so the failure appears as latency there, not as errors. What made inventory slow is not shown in the evidence.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-04e6b6244b44",
   "ev-46adbaf9ef22",
   "ev-b33c5ed2f4cc",
   "ev-2b50652f7ed1"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders appears to time out on inventory at about 2s, below inventory's p95 latency of about 4.76s. As a result, 100% of orders requests return 5xx.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-2b50652f7ed1",
    "ev-46adbaf9ef22",
    "ev-04e6b6244b44"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "The gateway propagates orders 504s as 502 on POST /checkout, giving an average 5xx ratio of 68.7%.",
