 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "The gateway 1.5.4 deploy is unlikely to be the cause. Errors were already present at 00:44:14, before the 00:45:44 deploy, and the gateway logged the same orders-504 error under both releases 1.4.2 and 1.5.4.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-7af1cda16e22",
    "ev-c7cb1f020e04",
    "ev-cffe79ea5fdb"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders is a propagator of the failure, not its origin. Its errors are timeouts waiting on inventory, and the time is spent in inventory self time.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-b33c5ed2f4cc",
    "ev-04e6b6244b44"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "The evidence does not show why inventory /reserve is slow. There is no inventory log pattern, no resource or database metrics, and no record of an inventory deploy.",
  "It is unknown when inventory latency started, because it was already elevated at window start. Earlier data would establish onset.",
  "It is unknown whether inventory release 3.1.5 was deployed recently. No inventory deployment record is in the snapshot."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Investigate inventory POST /reserve latency: look for an inventory deploy or config change, check its dependencies (e.g. the database or locks), and roll back or scale inventory if a cause is found.",
